vkstorm-core-rust licence
=========================

vkstorm-core-rust, the Rust core of the Vulkanstorm viewer, is dual-licensed.
You may use, modify and distribute it under either of these two licences, at
your choice:

  * the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 (LICENSE-LGPL-2.1), or
  * the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later
    version (LICENSE-GPL-3.0).

The crates port code of the Linden Lab Second Life viewer and of Firestorm,
which those projects license under LGPL-2.1 only:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only OR GPL-3.0-or-later

Section 3 of LGPL-2.1 lets any licensee apply the ordinary GNU GPL, version 2
or any newer version, to a copy instead; this repository offers that option
with GPL version 3 or later.

Code ported from other projects keeps its own licence beside the dual
licence: vkstorm-openjp2 (BSD-2-Clause, OpenJPEG and the openjp2 crate), the
libogg/libvorbis part of vkstorm-vorbis (BSD-3-Clause, LICENSE-xiph) and the
SoLoud part of vkstorm-audio (Zlib, LICENSE-soloud). Each crate's Cargo.toml
states its expression; NOTICE.md lists them and explains how to choose.

Source code: https://github.com/anne-skydancer/vkstorm-core-rust
